        "insufficient_evidence": false,
        "summary": "Mann describes Anthropic’s Responsible Scaling Policy as assessing societal risk at successive AI Safety Levels, with increasingly severe thresholds as models gain capability. The company also tests concrete risks in controlled settings, compares model assistance against prior methods, and shares findings so others can understand the risks.",
        "summary_citation_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S2",
          "S3"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "Risk tiers that rise with capability",
            "content": "Anthropic’s Responsible Scaling Policy defines AI Safety Levels to estimate the risk to society at each level of model intelligence. Mann says Anthropic considers itself at ASL-3, where there may be some risk of harm but not significant overall. ASL-4 involves the potential for significant loss of human life if a bad actor misuses the technology; ASL-5 could mean extinction-level harm through misuse or misalignment.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S1",
              "S2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Testing concrete risks under controlled conditions",
            "content": "For biological misuse, Anthropic assessed whether models could help create pandemics, comparing their biological uplift with Google Search—the previous state of the art in uplift trials—and brought in experts to evaluate these risks. Mann says ASL-3 models provided somewhat significant help to someone trying to create a bioweapon, while emphasizing that this is small compared with what future models might enable. He describes using the best models in laboratory settings to understand actual risks, rather than ignoring them and waiting for harm to occur in the wild.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S2",
              "S3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Communicating findings",
            "content": "Mann says Anthropic publishes its findings in part so other labs and legislators can understand the risks and what may happen as capabilities advance.",
            "citation_ids": [
              "S2",
              "S3"
            ]
          }
        ],
